#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""gh-pr-wait: wait for GitHub PR checks, reviews, merges, or events via GitHub Event Streams with slow safety-net re-checks and >= 60 s polling fallback.

  gh-pr-wait <PR_REF> [-R OWNER/REPO] [--for checks|review|merge|any] [--timeout DUR]
             [--safety-interval SECS] [--fallback-interval SECS] [--attach-timeout SECS]
             [--keep-subscription] [--allow-empty-checks] [--no-deadline] [--json] [--quiet]
  gh-pr-wait cleanup [--dry-run] [--all] [--json]

Uses GitHub Event Streams (`gh event subscription` + `gh event listen`, gh >= 2.105.0,
github.com PRs only) for event-driven wakeup with slow safety-net re-checks (clamped
>= 30 s, default 300 s) and automatic quota-safe polling fallback (>= 60 s interval) when
Event Streams is unavailable (non-github.com host, 403/422, older gh, attach timeout).

Operational invariants:
  - Attach-then-read: waits strictly for exact `Listening for events.` on stderr before
    the initial PR state read, and re-reads on reconnects.
  - Mode-specific, field-limited PR queries (never fetches untrusted review bodies):
      --for checks : `gh pr view --json=url,state,mergedAt,headRefOid,mergeable,statusCheckRollup`
      --for merge  : `gh pr view --json=url,state,mergedAt,headRefOid`
      --for any    : `gh pr view --json=url,state,mergedAt,headRefOid,statusCheckRollup`
      --for review : `gh api graphql` selecting only `url`, `state`, `mergedAt`,
                     `headRefOid`, and `reviews(last: 100) { nodes { id state submittedAt author { login } } }`
    Note: `statusCheckRollup` entries may include check descriptions from external apps;
    they are treated strictly as untrusted data and never echoed or followed.
  - Shared subscription coordination & best-effort stop-before-delete cleanup:
    Per canonical `(owner.lower(), repo.lower(), pr_number, sorted(events))` key, local
    waiters coordinate via an `flock`-locked refcount state file under
    `~/.local/state/djbclark-ade/gh-pr-wait` (`0700` dir, `0600` file, `GH_PR_WAIT_STATE_DIR`
    override) tracking `(pid, start_time)`. A listener is terminated (`SIGTERM` 5 s, then
    `SIGKILL` 5 s) and its reap MUST be proven before subscription deletion; if reap is
    unproven, ownership is shared/external/uncertain, or `--keep-subscription` is set,
    deletion is skipped (relying on the 24 h TTL + `gh-pr-wait cleanup`).
  - Cleanup caveat: `gh-pr-wait cleanup` checks PR state (`MERGED`/`CLOSED`) before
    deleting; that check-then-delete sequence is non-atomic (a closed PR could be reopened
    in the brief window before delete).

Exit codes:
  0    condition met (checks passed, new submitted review, PR merged, or valid event;
       or cleanup succeeded)
  1    condition failed (check failed, PR closed/merged before checks or review finished,
       PR closed without merge, or cleanup error)
  2    usage error or invalid PR reference / duration / flag value
  8    timeout reached before condition was met (matches `gh event listen`)
  124  stopped by external deadline enforcer (`deadline run`)
  128+N interrupted by signal N (e.g. 143 on SIGTERM, 130 on SIGINT)

Environment overrides:
  GH_BIN                         path to `gh` executable (default: `gh`)
  DEADLINE_BIN                   path to `deadline` executable (default: sibling `bin/deadline`)
  GH_PR_WAIT_STATE_DIR           directory for local subscription refcount/lock files
  GH_PR_WAIT_TEST_MIN_INTERVAL   test-only seam lowering safety/fallback/cooldown floors
  GH_PR_WAIT_TEST_STOP_TIMEOUT   test-only seam lowering listener stop wait (default 5 s)
"""
from __future__ import annotations

